# Line endings at checkout: cygwin bash scripts must stay LF, Notepad files CRLF,
# binary assets untouched.
# Note (S5-5): the eol rules apply at checkout only - files already materialized in a
# working tree are NOT re-smudged. A dirty re-clone (files written with the other eol)
# normalizes on fresh checkout: run `git checkout -- .` to re-materialize the tree,
# otherwise the working files keep their existing line endings.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=crlf
*.rc text eol=crlf
*.manifest text eol=crlf
*.ico binary
*.wav binary
